  "headline": "Groß leads Brighton's rout as the differentials cash in",
  "paragraphs": [
    "Brighton produced the biggest win of the season so far in Gameweek 4, beating Coventry City 5-0 away. Groß was at the centre of it with a goal, two assists and 17 points, the highest score of the week. Dunk also scored and joined him in the Dream Team with 12 points.",
    "It was a good week for managers who looked beyond the popular picks. Schade scored twice for Brentford and Bogle found the net for Leeds, each returning 15 points while owned by 3.5% and 2.2% of managers. Belloumi's two goals for Hull City brought 13 points at 1.0% ownership.",
    "The most-owned players did enough. João Pedro, in 74.3% of squads, scored and assisted in Chelsea's 2-2 draw with Hull City for 12 points. Haaland, the most-captained player, got the only goal in Man City's 1-0 win at Man Utd and 9 points. B.Fernandes, owned by 41.7%, managed 2 points after 615,807 more managers sold him than bought him before the deadline.",
    "There were four red cards, including one for Foden, who finished on -2 points. Raya saved a penalty and kept a clean sheet in Arsenal's 2-0 win at Sunderland, earning 14 points. The average manager scored 69 points, and 29 goals were scored across the 10 matches."
  ],
